[node name="Tutorial" type="Node" unique_id=1996116149]
process_mode = 1
script = ExtResource("1_auo41")
dialogue_intro = "Welcome to the combat tutorial.
[b]
The world of Hex Summons is full of threats so knowing how to fight is essential.
[b]
Combat encounters begin when you collide with another creature while traveling. Once you start a fight, you are locked in the encounter until you either win or fail.
[b]
To win you must simply lower the health of all opponents to zero. If all of your warriors' health drop to zero, you lose the fight and will be sent back to the title screen.
[b]
Your warriors and the enemies take turns executing their actions. The order of who goes next is indicated in the bar at the top of the screen."
dialogue_move = "Before we go over your arsenal, you must learn how to walk. On your warrior's turn you can select where they will move to using the {0}. You can select the target destination using {1}.
[b]
An indicator will appear showing the path they will take to reach the destination.
[b]
They will not move until you end their turn. You can do so by either selecting the option or by pressing its hotkey.
[b]
Practice taking your first steps. Move your warriors to the marked area when you are ready to learn about your arsenal."
dialogue_technique = "One way of dispatching of your foes is through the use of martial skills, or techniques.
[b]
All techniques have a cooldown, which is the number of turns that must pass before it can be used again. Some techniques have a cooldown of zero, meaning they can be used every turn.
[b]
Techniques and other actions have a range they can effect. This is indicated when you have it selected for use. Purple marks where the technique can be cast (its range). Yellow marks the area the technique effects (its area). Targets marked by the area will be hit by the technique.
[b]
Using a technique will end the warrior's turn. If you need to reposition you need to go back to movement. A technique will only be used if a target is within its area.
[b]
Master techniques and defeat the threat!"
dialogue_spell = "Another tool your warriors have is the power of spells. Spells are cast by expending elemental wisps, which come in one of four elements: earth, fire, water, and wind.
[b]
All spells have a requirement and a cost. In order to be able to cast it, the number of wisps the warrior has must meet the requirement value. When casting the spell, the cost value is paid from the warrior's wisp pool.
[b]
Wisps used for casting spells go into the summon pool. They cannot be used for casting spells while they are here.
[b]
Casting a spell ends the warrior's turn.
[b]
Harness your magical might and techniques to overcome the enemy!"
dialogue_summon = "The final power your warriors possess is the ability to call forth summons, entities of considerable strength.
[b]
In order to call a summon you need to have the required wisps stockpiled in the summon pool. When a summon is called, the required wisps are drawn from the summon pool to form it. Only one summon can be active at a time.
[b]
A summon bases its strength on the warrior who called it. The warrior's attack and defenses are multiplied. The warrior's health becomes the summon's; if it falls to zero the summon will fade and the warrior will be knocked out.
[b]
The active summon takes the turn of the warrior who called it, as they must use all of their focus to maintain the summon's form.
[b]
Whenever a summon uses an action it expends some of the wisps that make up its form. These wisps are returned to the warrior they were originally bonded with, allowing them to be used for spells again.
[b]
You now have access to your full arsenal. Harness the cycle of magic and claim your victory!"
tooltip_objective_movement = "Move to the indicated area."
tooltip_objective_technique = "Use your techniques to defeat the opponent."
tooltip_objective_spell = "Vanquish the foe using your spells and techniques."
tooltip_objective_summon = "Harness your full arsenal and finish the threat."
tooltip_movement_gamepad = "The camera will follow the tile selector. Use the right joystick to rotate the camera."
tooltip_movement_keymouse = "Hover the mouse at the edges of the screen to move the camera. Hold down {0} and drag the mouse to rotate the camera."

